    <string name="host_use_ipmi_power_help">The Power tab will use IPMI: status and power commands respond in a fraction of a second without opening an SSH session.</string>
    <string name="host_ipmi_privilege">Requested privilege level</string>
    <string name="host_ipmi_privilege_help">Operator is enough for power control and the UID LED; Read-only allows status checks. The iLO limits the level to the account\'s privileges, so an incomplete account is downgraded to read-only regardless of the requested level.</string>
    <string name="host_show_state_list">Show status in host list</string>
    <string name="host_show_state_list_help">The list will periodically query this host to show its power state and faults. IPMI is required; one SSH connection per host would be too slow and use up the iLO\'s limited sessions.</string>
    <string name="host_hardware_ipmi">Hardware tab via IPMI</string>
    <string name="host_hardware_ipmi_help">The Hardware tab will read IPMI sensors instead of walking the CLI tree. It is faster and needs no SSH session, but shows temperatures, fans, and power supplies rather than a detailed inventory.</string>
    <string name="host_always_open_ssh">Always open SSH session</string>
    <string name="host_always_open_ssh_help">When the Power tab uses IPMI, opening SSH in the background makes VSP, SSH, and Hardware immediately available. Useful when IPMI is read-only. This only applies when opening a host.</string>
    <string name="host_monitor_ipmi">Monitor over IPMI</string>
    <string name="host_monitor_ipmi_help">Each periodic check opens a new connection. SSH takes several seconds and uses one of the iLO\'s few sessions; IPMI exchanges a few UDP packets. IPMI alerts identify sensors rather than components.</string>
    <string name="host_ipmi_port">IPMI port (UDP)</string>
    <string name="host_ipmi_lan_help">IPMI/DCMI over LAN is disabled by default on iLO 3. Enable it on the iLO (Administration &gt; Access Settings), or this port will not respond.</string>
    <string name="host_ipmi_password_required">This host uses a private key and has no saved password. IPMI authenticates with a password; add one under Authentication or IPMI will not be used.</string>
    <string name="host_no_network_title">Network</string>
    <string name="host_no_network_help">No network configured. This server is reached directly. To use a tunnel, create a network using the Networks button on the home screen.</string>
    <string name="host_network_not_found">Network not found</string>
    <string name="host_network_missing_help">The network saved for this host no longer exists. Choose another network or direct access.</string>
