    <string name="instant_alert_test_explanation">“Test” asks the iLO to ping the phone, the network direction most likely to fail. It is the only test exposed by this CLI; a successful ping does not guarantee UDP port 162 will remain open.</string>
    <string name="instant_alert_listener_explanation">The phone listens for traps as soon as this mode is saved, using a persistent background service. Listening requires WireGuard: Android reserves port 162, and only the tunnel can open it.</string>
